BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heirloom & Harvest: The Art of the Pennsylvania Dutch Working Gard
 en
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T200000
UID:8ffe5ea44530a7a39064a6bfbbf9e4bd@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nStep back into 
 the 19th-century landscape of Pennsylvania Dutch Country\, where the soil 
 was a source of survival and the garden was a masterpiece of efficiency. T
 his program explores the striking divide between the ornamental excess of 
 the High Victorian Era and the rugged\, purposeful "Working Gardens" of th
 e Pennsylvania Germans. Through this deep dive\, the Pennsylvania Master G
 ardeners uncover the sustainable secrets of the past and translate them in
 to practical strategies for the modern back-to-the-land movement.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-program-173620
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
