SUMMARY:Skype-A-Scientist
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T180000
UID:061c7939eabe8cfcaaff75522c699d5e@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, STEM\, Everyone\n\nJoin us on May 21 for Skype-
 A-Scientist! Cortney Dean\, a research biologist\, ecologist and conservat
 ionist based in Wisconsin\, will give a brief talk about her work\, how sh
 e became a scientist\, and how her research affects us all. There will be 
 a Q&A session following where audience members are encouraged to ask quest
 ions. All ages welcome. Registration RequestedCortney Dean is a Conservati
 on Biologist and Independent Researcher living in Northern Wisconsin. She 
 studies how beavers impact ecosystems- including other animals like bats a
 nd birds\, water quality\, food webs\, and biodiversity. Her other scienti
 fic interests include wetlands\, nature based habitat restoration\, commun
 ity education\, and science communication. Outside of her research\, Cortn
 ey enjoys reading\, gardening\, hiking\, canoeing\, rockhounding\, and adv
 entures with her spouse and two dogs.
LOCATION:Adamstown\, ADM Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/skype-scientist-168970
