 How Big Were the Dinosaurs?Some dinosaurs\, such as the Barosaurus\, were 
 quite large and may have weighed as much as 35 tons. But other dinosaurs\,
  such as Compsognathus\, were about the size of a chicken and weighed only
  eight pounds. Join a Naturalist from Lancaster County Park to learn just 
 how big they were in comparison to modern day creatures and landmarks by c
 ompleting activities and putting your knowledge to the test!Ages 8-12
LOCATION:Strasburg-Heisler
