DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Everyone\n\nJoin our epic adventure to The La
 nd Down Under! The Didgeridoo Down Under Show is an energetic fusion of Au
 stralian music\, culture\, comedy\, character building\, storytelling\, an
 d loads of audience movement and participation. The didgeridoo has been pl
 ayed by Aboriginal Australians for at least 1\,500 years\, and it's known 
 for its otherworldly sound. We'll explore the Outback and the Great Barrie
 r Reef\, we'll unearth Aboriginal artwork and artifacts\, we’ll learn ab
 out amazing creatures like kangaroos and koalas ... and much more ... all 
 while moving and grooving to the pulsing rhythms of the didge. The DDU Sho
 w is interactive\, educational\, motivational and super fun for all ages!P
 rogram will be held at St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church in their Fel
 lowship Hall. Please enter on the 6th Street side at the red doors.Part of
  our 2026 Summer Reading program series.
LOCATION:Columbia
